11.27:
He who earnestly seeks good, seeks what is pleasing; 
But to him who seeks evil, 
It comes to him.

14.21:
He who despises his neighbor sins; 
But he who shows favor to the poor, 
O ashrĕ is he.

16.17:
The highway of the straight 
Is to turn away from evil; 
He who guards his ḥai watches over His Way.

18.20:
A man’s stomach is satisfied 
From the fruit of his mouth; 
He is satisfied by the increase of his lips.

19.7:
All the brothers of the poor shall hate him; 
How much more shall his friends go far from him! 
He pursues promises - they are gone!

19.19:
One of great wrath bears punishment; 
For if you rescue, 
You only have to do it again.

19.25:
Beat a scoffer, and the simple is made wise; 
And reprove one who has understanding, 
And he discerns knowledge.

20.19:
He who goes about as a slanderer reveals secrets; 
Therefore do not associate with him 
Who speaks smoothly with his lips.

21.1:
The meleḵ’s heart is as channels of water 
In the hand of 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄; 
He turns it wherever He wants.

22.18:
For they are pleasant 
If you guard them within you; 
Let all of them be ready on your lips.

23.5:
Do you lay your eyes on that which is not? 
For riches certainly make themselves wings; 
They fly away like an eagle to the shamayim.

23.31:
Do not look on the wine when it is red, 
When it gives its color in the cup, 
As it flows smoothly;

24.14:
Know that wisdom is thus to your being; 
If you have found it, there is a future, 
And your expectancy is not cut off.

24.15:
Do not lie in wait, O wicked, 
Against the dwelling of the righteous; 
Do not ravage his resting place;

24.27:
Prepare your work outside, 
And make it fit for yourself in the field; 
Then you shall build your house.

24.31:
And see, it was all overgrown with thorns; 
Its surface was covered with nettles; 
And its stone wall was broken down.

28.10:
He who causes the straight to go astray in an evil way, 
Falls into his own pit; 
But the perfect inherit the good.

30.8:
Remove falsehood and a lying word far from me; 
Give me neither poverty nor riches; 
Feed me my portion of bread;

31.4:
Not for melaḵim, O Lemu’ĕl, 
Not for melaḵim to drink wine, 
Nor for princes to desire strong drink;

4.4:
Then he taught me and said to me, 
“Let your heart hold fast my words; 
Guard my Commands, and live.

7.23:
Till an arrow strikes through his liver; 
Like a bird rushing into a snare, 
And did not know it would take his ḥai.
